-- title:
--   Freeness of the formal plane over invariant generators
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B$ a commutative ring and write $A = B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ for `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) B`. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$ in the sense of `FormalODModule`, i.e. a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F = X.F$ together with an action of `Zp2 p` by endomorphisms of $F$ and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ[a] = [\sigma a]\circ\varpi$; of this data only the law $F$ enters the statement. Let $I \subseteq A$ be an ideal for which some power $q$ has $x_i^q \in I$ for both $i$, let $\iota$ be a finite index type, let $bC$ be a $B$-basis of $A/I$ indexed by $\iota$, and let $b : \iota \to A$ be a family whose classes modulo $I$ are the $bC_k$. Let $m$ be a natural number and $u_0,\dots,u_{m-1} \in A$ power series with vanishing constant coefficient, each invariant in the sense that $\mathrm{subst}\,F.toPowerSeries\,(u_j) - u_j(x)$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by the image of $I$ under $x \mapsto y$, and suppose the $u_j$ generate $I$. Then, writing $c(u)$ for substitution of the $u_j$ into $c \in B[\![T_0,\dots,T_{m-1}]\!]$: every $f \in A$ is of the form $\sum_{k} c_k(u)\, b_k$ for some $c : \iota \to B[\![T]\!]$, and whenever $\sum_k c_k(u)\, b_k = 0$ one has $c_k(u) = 0$ for every $k$.
--
--   This is the freeness statement underlying a free formal-group action: the formal plane over $B$ is free, with basis the lifted classes $b_k$, over the subring generated by any family of invariant generators of the ideal $I$ cutting out the subgroup. The uniqueness clause is stated for the substituted series $c_k(u)$ rather than for the coefficient series $c_k$ themselves. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_span_range_eq_of_le_span_setOf_invariant_of_field`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_span_range_eq_of_le_span_setOf_invariant_of_field).
